From 988316e689774a9c8959f2b32021c2d70d957b0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:59:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplmesh: whm: fix radar detection event mapping, delivery,
 and DFS state tracking

The whm backend did not reliably report radar-triggered DFS channels in
the Channel Preference Report's CAC Status/Completion Report TLV. This
was caused by four separate issues:

1. Missing event mapping

   wpaCtrl_to_bwl_event() did not translate the "DFS-RADAR-DETECTED"
   opcode to any beerocks event; it fell through to Event::Invalid
   and was silently dropped by the default case in
   process_wpa_ctrl_event().

2. Missing/unreliable event delivery

   "DFS-RADAR-DETECTED" is fired on the AccessPoint/VAP path. The
   existing subscription handler for AP-path wpaCtrl events discards
   any event whose path is not yet present in the agent's internal
   VAP-info map (e.g. during early boot, before VAP info has been
   populated), so the event could be dropped before even reaching the
   opcode mapping above.

3. DFS state never updated for radar-triggered channels

   refresh_radio_info() derives each channel's DFS state only while
   iterating the platform's reported list of currently possible
   channels. When a channel is hit by radar, the platform may remove
   it from that list entirely instead of keeping it listed with a
   radar/non-occupancy marker. Because the loop only visited the
   possible-channels list, a radar-hit channel removed from it was
   never visited, so its DFS state was never updated to reflect the
   radar detection.

4. Timing race between the channel-switch notification and the
   platform's radar-channel data becoming available

   The platform populates its radar-triggered-channels data and
   fires its channel-switch/CSA notification as two independent,
   loosely-synchronized events. The agent previously relied solely on
   the channel-switch notification to trigger a refresh of its
   channel/radio info and the subsequent Channel Preference Report
   rebuild. When the radar-triggered-channels data had not yet been
   updated by the time that refresh ran, the resulting report could
   be built from stale data, omitting the just-detected radar
   channels entirely - even though all of the above issues were
   otherwise fixed.

Together, these issues meant that a radar detection - whether or not
it was accompanied by an immediate channel switch - could fail to be
reflected in the agent's channel/radio state and could fail to
produce a correctly populated CAC Status/Completion Report TLV.

This change:

- Adds an explicit mapping for "DFS-RADAR-DETECTED" to
  Event::DFS_RADAR_Detected, and handles it by recording the channel
  switch reason as Radar and pushing the event through the normal
  event queue. This reuses the existing shared handling for
  DFS_RADAR_Detected/ACS_Completed/CSA_Finished, which refreshes the
  radio info and propagates the notification further up the stack.

- Adds a dedicated event subscription for "DFS-RADAR-DETECTED" on all
  AccessPoint paths, independent of the current state of the VAP-info
  map, so the event is reliably forwarded to the wpaCtrl event handler
  regardless of VAP-info population timing. This follows the same
  pattern already used for AWGN interference detection, which has the
  same underlying delivery characteristics.

- Fixes refresh_radio_info() to derive each channel's DFS state from
  the union of the platform's possible-channels list and its
  radar-triggered-channels list, instead of the possible-channels
  list alone. This guarantees a radar-hit channel's DFS state is
  always updated to reflect the radar detection, even if the platform
  has removed that channel from the possible-channels list.

- Adds a dedicated subscription directly on the platform's
  radar-triggered-channels parameter, independent of the
  channel-switch notification. Whenever that data changes, the agent
  refreshes its radio/channel info and re-triggers the Channel
  Preference Report rebuild with guaranteed-current data, removing
  the dependency on any particular ordering between the two
  independent platform events.

- Additionally, a channel-change event whose reason indicates a
  radar-driven change is now always treated as such, instead of only
  being accepted when a specific prior internal state had been armed
  by an earlier CAC failure on the same radio - avoiding a case where
  a radar-driven channel change with no such preceding CAC failure
  was previously dropped entirely.

No functional changes are introduced to the nl80211 backend or to any
other part of the agent; only the missing event mapping and its
handler, the dedicated subscriptions, and the DFS-state derivation fix
are added for the whm backend.

Signed-off-by: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.cpp   | 80 ++++++++++++++++++-
 common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.h     |  1 +
 common/beerocks/bwl/whm/base_wlan_hal_whm.cpp | 57 +++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 129 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.cpp b/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.cpp
index 0851303..eb0f1ea 100644
--- a/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.cpp
+++ b/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.cpp
@@ -100,6 +100,12 @@ static ap_wlan_hal::Event wpaCtrl_to_bwl_event(const std::string &opcode)
         return ap_wlan_hal::Event::ACS_Completed;
     } else if (opcode == "ACS-FAILED") {
         return ap_wlan_hal::Event::ACS_Failed;
+    } else if (opcode == "DFS-RADAR-DETECTED") {
+        // Surface radar detection as an explicit event, independent of whether
+        // a channel switch follows, matching the nl80211 backend behavior.
+        LOG(WARNING) << "[RADAR-DBG] wpaCtrl_to_bwl_event: matched DFS-RADAR-DETECTED opcode"
+                     << " -> mapping to Event::DFS_RADAR_Detected";
+        return ap_wlan_hal::Event::DFS_RADAR_Detected;
     }
 
     return ap_wlan_hal::Event::Invalid;
@@ -151,6 +157,7 @@ ap_wlan_hal_whm::ap_wlan_hal_whm(const std::string &iface_name, hal_event_cb_t c
     subscribe_to_ap_mgmt_frame_events();
     subscribe_to_afc_update_events();
     subscribe_to_awgn_events();
+    subscribe_to_radar_events();
 }
 
 ap_wlan_hal_whm::~ap_wlan_hal_whm() {}
@@ -1708,6 +1715,43 @@ void ap_wlan_hal_whm::subscribe_to_awgn_events()
     m_ambiorix_cl.subscribe_to_object_event(wbapi_utils::search_path_ap(), event_handler, filter);
 }
 
+void ap_wlan_hal_whm::subscribe_to_radar_events()
+{
+    // Subscribe to wpaCtrlEvents on ALL AccessPoint paths without VAP filtering.
+    // DFS-RADAR-DETECTED is fired on the VAP/AccessPoint path. The standard
+    // subscribe_to_ap_events() handler drops any event whose path is not yet present in
+    // m_vapsExtInfo (e.g. during early boot, before VAP info has been populated) - the same
+    // class of issue already fixed for AWGN via subscribe_to_awgn_events(). This dedicated
+    // subscription ensures DFS-RADAR-DETECTED is always forwarded to process_wpa_ctrl_event(),
+    // independent of the current state of m_vapsExtInfo.
+    auto event_handler        = std::make_shared<sAmbiorixEventHandler>();
+    event_handler->event_type = AMX_CL_WPA_CTRL_EVT;
+
+    event_handler->callback_fn = [this](AmbiorixVariant &event_data) -> void {
+        std::string event_str;
+        if (!event_data.read_child<>(event_str, "eventData") || event_str.empty()) {
+            return;
+        }
+
+        // Only handle DFS-RADAR-DETECTED events
+        if (event_str.find("DFS-RADAR-DETECTED") == std::string::npos) {
+            return;
+        }
+
+        LOG(WARNING) << "[RADAR-DBG] subscribe_to_radar_events: DFS-RADAR-DETECTED received"
+                     << " -> calling process_wpa_ctrl_event";
+        process_wpa_ctrl_event(event_data);
+    };
+
+    // Subscribe to all AP paths - no VAP filter restriction
+    std::string filter = "(path matches '" + wbapi_utils::search_path_ap() +
+                         "[0-9]+.$') && (notification == '" + AMX_CL_WPA_CTRL_EVT + "')";
+
+    LOG(WARNING) << "[RADAR-DBG] subscribe_to_radar_events: filter=" << filter
+                 << " radio=" << get_iface_name();
+    m_ambiorix_cl.subscribe_to_object_event(wbapi_utils::search_path_ap(), event_handler, filter);
+}
+
 bool ap_wlan_hal_whm::simulate_awgn()
 {
     // Trigger AWGN simulation on the WHM platform by invoking the DCS.Simulation RPC method
@@ -2802,6 +2846,18 @@ bool ap_wlan_hal_whm::process_radio_event(const std::string &interface, const st
         LOG(WARNING) << "request updating vaps list of radio " << interface;
         event_queue_push(Event::APS_update_list);
         return true;
+    } else if (key == "RadarTriggeredDfsChannels") {
+        // Fired when the platform's RadarTriggeredDfsChannels list is actually updated.
+        // Refresh the full channel/radio info now that the data is guaranteed to be
+        // current (see subscribe_to_radio_events() for why relying solely on the prior
+        // CSA/channel-switch notification can race ahead of this list being populated),
+        // then re-trigger the same Radar-reason notification path used for an explicit
+        // DFS-RADAR-DETECTED event, so a Channel Preference Report rebuild is requested
+        // with the now-current radar/NOL channel data.
+        refresh_radio_info();
+        m_radio_info.last_csa_sw_reason = ChanSwReason::Radar;
+        event_queue_push(Event::DFS_RADAR_Detected);
+        return true;
     }
     return true;
 }
@@ -2824,10 +2880,16 @@ bool ap_wlan_hal_whm::process_radio_channel_change_event(const AmbiorixVariant *
     if (chan_change_reason != "MANUAL" && chan_change_reason != "AUTO") {
         LOG(INFO) << "chan_change_reason other than MANUAL or AUTO:" << chan_change_reason;
 
-        // Handle DFS channel changes
-        if (chan_change_reason == "DFS" && m_accept_dfs_channel_change_after_cac_failure) {
-            LOG(INFO) << "Channel change event received following a failed CAC_Completed, "
-                      << "handling it as part of the radar flow...";
+        // Handle DFS channel changes. A "DFS" reason always indicates a radar-driven
+        // channel change (whether or not it was preceded by a CAC failure on this
+        // radio) and must always be accepted and forwarded as Radar - previously this
+        // was only accepted when m_accept_dfs_channel_change_after_cac_failure had been
+        // armed by a prior CAC failure, causing a radar-driven channel change with no
+        // such preceding CAC failure to fall through to the "Unsupported channel change
+        // reason" branch below and be dropped entirely (no CSA notification at all).
+        if (chan_change_reason == "DFS") {
+            LOG(INFO) << "Channel change event received due to a radar-driven DFS channel "
+                      << "change, handling it as part of the radar flow...";
             m_accept_dfs_channel_change_after_cac_failure = false;
             m_radio_info.last_csa_sw_reason               = ChanSwReason::Radar;
         }
@@ -3487,6 +3549,16 @@ bool ap_wlan_hal_whm::process_wpa_ctrl_event(const beerocks::wbapi::AmbiorixVari
         event_queue_push(Event::DFS_NOP_Finished, msg_buff);
         break;
     }
+    case Event::DFS_RADAR_Detected: {
+        // Radar detection is independent of any channel switch that may or may not
+        // follow it. Always record the reason as Radar and push the event so the
+        // shared DFS_RADAR_Detected/ACS_Completed/CSA_Finished handling refreshes
+        // the radio info and notifies the rest of the stack, keeping behavior
+        // consistent with the nl80211 backend.
+        m_radio_info.last_csa_sw_reason = ChanSwReason::Radar;
+        event_queue_push(event);
+        break;
+    }
     case Event::CSA_Finished: {
         const std::string reason  = parsed_obj["reason"];
         ChanSwReason chanSwReason = ChanSwReason::Unknown;
diff --git a/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.h b/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.h
index 58b22f7..73fd9c5 100644
--- a/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.h
+++ b/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/ap_wlan_hal_whm.h
@@ -314,6 +314,7 @@ private:
      * when wld sends them with a mismatched path.
      */
     void subscribe_to_awgn_events();
+    void subscribe_to_radar_events();
 
     /**
      * @brief Process event "BSS-TM-RESP"
diff --git a/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/base_wlan_hal_whm.cpp b/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/base_wlan_hal_whm.cpp
index fd084ee..a5396c2 100644
--- a/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/base_wlan_hal_whm.cpp
+++ b/common/beerocks/bwl/whm/base_wlan_hal_whm.cpp
@@ -114,6 +114,32 @@ void base_wlan_hal_whm::subscribe_to_radio_events()
 
     m_ambiorix_cl.subscribe_to_object_event(wifi_radio_channel_path, event_handler,
                                             filter_radio_channel);
+
+    // Subscribe directly to RadarTriggeredDfsChannels parameter changes on ChannelMgt.
+    // The platform may populate this list a short time after the channel-switch/CSA
+    // notification fires (both are driven by independent, loosely-synchronized events on
+    // the platform side). Relying solely on the CSA/channel-switch notification to trigger
+    // a radio-info refresh can therefore race ahead of this list actually being updated,
+    // resulting in a refresh that misses the just-detected radar channels. Subscribing
+    // directly to this parameter removes that race: the refresh (and the resulting
+    // Channel Preference Report rebuild) is triggered exactly when the data becomes
+    // available, regardless of its timing relative to any channel-switch event.
+    std::string channel_mgt_obj_path       = m_radio_path + "ChannelMgt.";
+    std::string filter_radar_triggered_chs = "(path matches '" + channel_mgt_obj_path +
+                                             "$')"
+                                             " && (notification == '" +
+                                             AMX_CL_OBJECT_CHANGED_EVT +
+                                             "')"
+                                             " && (contains('parameters.RadarTriggeredDfsChannels'))";
+
+    auto radar_channels_event_handler        = std::make_shared<sAmbiorixEventHandler>();
+    radar_channels_event_handler->event_type = AMX_CL_OBJECT_CHANGED_EVT;
+    radar_channels_event_handler->callback_fn = [this](AmbiorixVariant &event_data) -> void {
+        process_radio_event(get_iface_name(), "RadarTriggeredDfsChannels", nullptr);
+    };
+
+    m_ambiorix_cl.subscribe_to_object_event(channel_mgt_obj_path, radar_channels_event_handler,
+                                            filter_radar_triggered_chs);
 }
 
 void base_wlan_hal_whm::subscribe_to_radio_channel_change_events()
@@ -831,16 +857,37 @@ bool base_wlan_hal_whm::refresh_radio_info()
 
     if (radio->read_child(s_val, "PossibleChannels")) {
         auto channels_vec = beerocks::string_utils::str_split(s_val, ',');
-        for (auto &chan_str : channels_vec) {
+
+        // pWHM may remove a channel from PossibleChannels entirely once radar is
+        // detected on it (rather than keeping the channel listed with a NOL/radar
+        // marker). If that channel is only iterated from channels_vec below, it is
+        // silently skipped and its entry in m_radio_info.channels_list is left at
+        // its previous (stale, non-UNAVAILABLE) dfs_state - meaning a radar/NOL
+        // channel is never reported via the CAC Status Report TLV's detected-pairs
+        // (non-occupancy) list. To guarantee every radar-triggered channel is always
+        // reflected with dfs_state=UNAVAILABLE regardless of its current presence in
+        // PossibleChannels, iterate the union of channels_vec and
+        // radar_triggered_channels_set below instead of channels_vec alone.
+        std::unordered_set<std::string> union_channels_set(channels_vec.begin(),
+                                                            channels_vec.end());
+        union_channels_set.insert(radar_triggered_channels_set.begin(),
+                                  radar_triggered_channels_set.end());
+
+        for (auto &chan_str : union_channels_set) {
+            if (chan_str.empty()) {
+                continue;
+            }
             uint32_t chanNum   = beerocks::string_utils::stoi(chan_str);
             auto &channel_info = m_radio_info.channels_list[chanNum];
 
             if (son::wireless_utils::is_dfs_channel(chanNum, m_radio_info.frequency_band)) {
-                if (cleared_channels_set.find(chan_str) != cleared_channels_set.end()) {
-                    channel_info.dfs_state = beerocks::eDfsState::AVAILABLE;
-                } else if (radar_triggered_channels_set.find(chan_str) !=
-                           radar_triggered_channels_set.end()) {
+                if (radar_triggered_channels_set.find(chan_str) !=
+                    radar_triggered_channels_set.end()) {
+                    // Radar/NOL takes priority over any (possibly stale) cleared-channel
+                    // membership for the same channel number.
                     channel_info.dfs_state = beerocks::eDfsState::UNAVAILABLE;
+                } else if (cleared_channels_set.find(chan_str) != cleared_channels_set.end()) {
+                    channel_info.dfs_state = beerocks::eDfsState::AVAILABLE;
                 } else {
                     channel_info.dfs_state = beerocks::eDfsState::USABLE;
                 }
